  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Rural Women&#x2019;s Participation in Good and inclusive local Governance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">General trends in the Sierra Leonean political and governance scene indicate that women continue to significantly lag behind in representation at all levels.
Political party leaders and strategists argue that very few women aspire for political or community leadership positions and the few that do so lack the requisite education, skill and the charisma to succeed. 
The project intends to educate communities so women are able to participate, transform systems to improve women&#x2019;s right; and move beyond the traditional economic empowerment of women. Specifically the project will build the capacities of local women to participate in local governance systems: chiefdom and district levels.</narrative>
  </description>
